description: Unit vs integration vs e2e IO rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Test layers

- **Unit** (`npm test` / default `cargo test` / `dotnet test` unit projects): core, generators, sqlite, and memory only. No other providers, dialects, or samples. No I/O. Mocks, fakes, in-memory ports. No filesystem, network, Docker, or real database engines.
- **Integration**: limited I/O only. In-process engines (e.g. SQLite command YAML specs), no Docker, no remote servers.
- **E2E** (`test:e2e`, `test:e2e:ci`, `test:e2e:rust`, `test:e2e:csharp`, `test:e2e:sqlite`, `test:samples`): dialects, other providers, and samples. Real functional tests and/or Docker.

Do not add provider or sample suites back into unit `npm test`. `scripts/unit-test-scope.test.mjs` fails if `package.json` or `typescript/package.json` `scripts.test` names another provider, `test:samples`, `test:e2e`, `--workspaces`, or `npm run build`. Do not put repository CRUD or other real functional suites in unit tests. Do not call Docker or `MYSQL_URL`/`POSTGRES_URL` from unit tests.
